 "fixes": {
  "save_entry_points": "Pause-menu Save/Load and the displayed path use day1a_slot0.json in Day-1A mode (main.gd routes them to the Day-1A adapter; the proof's QA reset/study jumps are refused there). F5/F9, autosaves, the menu and a fresh launch share one adapter path. A seeded proof slot0.json and slot0.json.bak stay byte-identical through repeated menu/key saves and loads in one process and across six relaunched processes.",
  "scene_resumption": "Save schema 2 keeps queued lines (time to presentation), the open choice and its options, every actor's position/route/activity/arrival tag/facing (the community included), mule trails, seat and halter, and beat state containing vectors/arrays. The adapter replaces the scene and resynchronises body and seat, figures, mules, bell queue, office transport, HUD (subtitles, replies), prompt and end card (_ended). An earlier slot loaded after the end card resumes; an end autosave loaded on a fresh launch shows the card and stays stopped. Schema 1 (e223bc2) is read explicitly: the community, awaited arrivals and interrupted line sequences of the beat are rebuilt and the load reports it.",
  "nones": "No load places anyone: brothers keep their positions, activities and remaining routes at the bell, while walking, in the choir and afterwards; a restored bell rings only the strokes still due; the office (chant) begins only when the brothers are in their stalls; after the office everyone leaves the choir.",
  "names": "Lines carry `teaches` (checked against the line text); a name is learned when that line is presented. An interrupted, unheard introduction teaches nothing.",
  "tests": "The disabled `or true` assertion is replaced by a check that restore places nobody. A restored director must match the uninterrupted day for 60 s after saves at 13 moments (max deviation 0.0 m). New domain tests: halter hold, bell remainder, names, schema-1 migration. New scene suite on the real main scene: menu, F5/F9, interrupted meal and end, repeated loads into used objects, Nones stages, seat/carry/hold, six separate-process relaunches. Both, and the PM probes, gate build_phase1.sh.",
  "william_walk": "Walk playback is calibrated from the planted foot's median backward speed in each clip (0.62–0.65 m/s for the walks, not the 0.50–0.55 previously measured), keeping planted feet planted for every walker. William (scenario stride 1.25, knee_ease) lengthens his step as he quickens instead of only raising cadence, eases the clip's deepest knee bend above 50°, and lowers the pelvis so the planted foot keeps the ground. Lead/wait, speed and lines unchanged; the body remains a stand-in.",
  "benchmarks": "The residency loop approaches the gate court unmeasured, completes a whole warm-up loop, then measures. Raw frames (wall clock, loop, leg, pipeline compilations), per-second engine counters and epoch-stamped external RSS are retained and aligned; frames over 50 ms record their context (compilations that frame, engine process/physics time, window focus, director events, place)."
 },
 "cold_stall_investigation": {
  "question": "Two 541–591 ms frames in the free period of the first run of the e223bc2-era package (5 Oct) were provisionally attributed to first-use shader/pipeline compilation.",
  "trials": "Fresh export from 4c16e99/fb12412 code. A: never-run binary, Godot shader cache moved aside (cold). B: immediately again (warm). C: Godot shader cache moved aside again with the binary already run (Metal system cache warm). Each: the whole slice, real time, 1920×1080, VSync off, no other GPU job. D: the candidate package exported from 60ec496 (new binary, Godot cache as left by C).",
  "findings": [
   "A (cold): 116.2 FPS, p95 11.17 ms, max 35.1 ms, no frame over 50 ms. 19 pipeline compilations occurred while measuring (most in the first ~70 s, one at 277 s); none coincided with a frame over 36 ms.",
   "B (warm): 114.0 FPS, p95 11.46 ms, max 1081 ms; frames over 50 ms: meal 53/54/67 ms, free 1081 ms (762 s in) and 57 ms. No pipeline compilation, director event, counter change or RSS change at any of them; RSS fell ~190 MiB (498 to 304) about 20 s after the 1081 ms frame.",
   "C (Godot cache removed again, Metal cache warm): 127.8 FPS, p95 11.31 ms, max 36.0 ms, no frame over 50 ms; the same 19 compilations.",
   "D (candidate package): 103.5 FPS, p95 11.19 ms, max 21.2 ms, no frame over 50 ms; the same 19 compilations; the spike instrumentation had nothing to record.",
   "The walk calibration added to the figures costs 1.5-2 ms once per clip at first use, not hundreds.",
   "Frame rate and counted renderer work (draw calls, primitives) differ between runs on the same legs and can shift within a run (ten-loop run: 108 FPS for loops 1-9, 123 in loop 10; soak: 145 with about 40% fewer draw calls on the same legs). Route, visible figures, pipelines and memory do not explain it; not diagnosed."
  ],
  "conclusion": "The 5 October 541/591 ms stalls are not reproduced in two cold runs or the candidate's first run, and first-use shader/pipeline compilation produced no long frame in any trial; that attribution is withdrawn. The one long frame seen (1081 ms, warm run) has no identified cause: no compilation, game event or memory event coincided with it. Frames over 50 ms now also record engine process/physics time and window focus/minimised state (runner 60ec496) so the next occurrence can be placed inside or outside the engine.",
  "loading_time_preparation": "Not added: no measurement showed first-use compilation causing a stall, so no loading-time preparation was introduced."
 },
